      "math_academy_id": "e-14216",
      "problem": "Solve the equation $\\left\\vert 7x \\right\\vert = 21.$",
      "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|7x| = 7x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7x| & =21 \\\\ 7x & =21 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|7x| = -7x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7x| & =21 \\\\ -7x & =21 \\\\ \\frac{-7x}{-7} & =\\frac{21}{-7} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=3$ and $x=-3.$ We can write this more compactly as $x = \\pm 3.$",
